old loop (for checking syntax of or executing instructions in a content stream):
```
while (read_instruction())
{
    if(keyword is ...)
        ...
    else if(keyword is m/re)
    {
        execute m/re;
        while(true)
        {
            assert(read_instruction());
            if(keyword is m/re/l/c/v/y/h)
                execute m/re/l/c/v/y/h;
            else if(keyword is S/s/f/F/f*/B/B*/b/b*/n)
            {
                execute S/s/f/F/f*/B/B*/b/b*/n;
                break;
            }
            else if(keyword is W/W*)
            {
                execute W/W*;
                assert(read_instruction());
                if(keyword is S/s/f/F/f*/B/B*/b/b*/n)
                {
                    execute S/s/f/F/f*/B/B*/b/b*/n;
                    break;
                }
                else
                    error: unexpected keyword;
            }
            else
                error: unexpected keyword;
        }
    }
    else
        error: unexpected keyword;
}
```
new loop:
```
while (true)
{
    bool has_instruction = read_instruction();
peeked_instruction:;
    if(!has_instruction)
        break;
    if(keyword is ...)
        ...
    else if(keyword is m/re)
    {
        execute m/re;
        while(true)
        {
            assert(read_instruction());
            if(keyword is m/re/l/c/v/y/h)
                execute m/re/l/c/v/y/h;
            else if(keyword is S/s/F/B/B*/b/b*/n)
            {
                execute S/s/F/B/B*/b/b*/n;
                break;
            }
            else if(keyword is f/f*)
            {
                execute f/f*;
                has_instruction = read_instruction();
                if(has_instruction && keyword is S)
                {
                    execute S;
                    has_instruction = read_instruction();
                }
                goto peeked_instruction;
            }
            else if(keyword is W/W*)
            {
                execute W/W*;
                assert(read_instruction());
                if(keyword is S/s/F/B/B*/b/b*/n)
                {
                    execute S/s/F/B/B*/b/b*/n;
                    break;
                }
                else if(keyword is f/f*)
                {
                    execute f/f*;
                    has_instruction = read_instruction();
                    if(has_instruction && keyword is S)
                    {
                        execute S;
                        has_instruction = read_instruction();
                    }
                    goto peeked_instruction;
                }
                else
                    error: unexpected keyword;
            }
            else
                error: unexpected keyword;
        }
    }
    else
        error: unexpected keyword;
}
```

`9.7.6.2 CMap mapping` does not take into account these situations: "what happens when codespace is empty", "what happens when number of remaining bytes is less than length of shortest CID_range(s)".
(`Adobe Technical Note #5014, Adobe CMap and CIDFont Files Specification` does not require that `begincodespacerange` appears or `begincodespacerange` defines non-zero number of ranges.)
CMap mapping logic:
```
if(there are 0 codespace ranges)
    result in nothing? result in "number of bytes in show_string" CIDs of value 0? result in "number of bytes in show_string divided by length of shortest CID_range(s)" CIDs of value 0?
else
{
    while(show_string's remaining number of bytes != 0)
    {
        if(show_string's remaining number of bytes < length of shortest CID_range(s))
            result in nothing? result in 1 CID of value 0? result in "number of bytes in show_string" CIDs of value 0?
        else
        {
            length_of_longest_length_partial_match_so_far = 0;
            range_length_of_range_having_longest_length_partial_match_so_far = length of shortest CID_range(s);
            ... (for CID_range(s) of increasing length, find longest-length partial match, if the partial match is a full match then break)
            ... (select character using bytes)
            ... (consume bytes from show_string)
        }
    }
}
```

**`Unicode`** `U+0004`'s **`Unicode character name or (alternative alias)`** should change from `(END OF TEXT)` to `(End of Transmission)`;
**`Unicode`** `U+0005`'s **`Unicode character name or (alternative alias)`** should change from `(End of Transmission)` to `(Enquiry)`;
**`Unicode`** `U+02D8`'s **`Character`** should change from `u` to `˘`;
**`Unicode`** `U+02C7`'s **`Character`** should change from `v` to `ˇ`;

In clause 13.7.1 General, replace the single long sentence that starts with “Such features as:” with a bullet list that enumerates each feature separately. For example:

Such features include:
• controlling when the presentation is activated and deactivated;
• providing scripts that control the presentation;
• specifying viewing parameters, such as lighting and camera angles (for example, for interactive 3D presentations);
• specifying animation parameters, such as speed and looping behaviour;
• supplying assets, including the base video, audio and animation files, as well as any required auxiliary files (for example, scripts);
• determining how the rich media annotation relates to the page display (for example, within a fixed rectangle on the page or in its own window);
• specifying configuration details for toolbars, navigation and other controls.

This change keeps the technical content intact while improving clarity and aligning with list-based presentations used elsewhere in the standard.

